{"id": "L14", "command": "submit", "inputs": {"recommendation": {"decision": "keep", "challenger": null, "diagnosis": "The champion improved overall in development, but India got worse while Mexico improved, and Mexico's customer markup has moved recently. A ridge model on markup features beat the champion consistently across corridors, but its risk band was too wide in the promotion window, so the rule does not allow a switch.", "evidence": [{"claim": "The champion's error over the last 26 weeks was 60.26 bps vs 63.75 bps before (-5.47%), but India worsened from 17.97 bps to 34.78 bps.", "ledger_ids": ["L02"]}, {"claim": "The markup-only ridge model with all history had 55.75 bps error vs the champion's 60.26 bps (-7.48%), and was lower in every corridor: MX 60.56 bps vs 67.6 bps, IN 32.78 bps vs 34.78 bps, BR 73.77 bps vs 78.26 bps.", "ledger_ids": ["L10"]}, {"claim": "Markup was the driver: ridge on markup alone with a 2y window improved error by -6.7%, while lagged residuals alone improved it by only -0.73%.", "ledger_ids": ["L07", "L08"]}, {"claim": "In the promotion window the challenger had 45.34 bps error vs the champion's 50.79 bps (-10.73%) with a DM p-value of 0.021, but its band breach rate of 1.2% is outside 2%-9%, so the promotion test failed.", "ledger_ids": ["L13"]}], "risks": "Keeping the champion leaves a consistent accuracy gain unused; the markup model's lower error looks real, and the champion's India error has been drifting up. The challenger's band may simply be miscalibrated rather than the model being worse.", "watch_next_week": "Watch India error for the champion and whether Mexico's markup keeps shifting. Re-test a markup-feature challenger, checking its band breach rate is within the allowed range before using the promotion test."}}, "result": {"accepted": true, "errors": [], "attempt": 1}, "time": "2026-11-15T13:43:22Z"}
